  <article class="container">
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="tag">VPN</span>
      <h1>ExpressVPN vs NordVPN: Which VPN Is Better in 2026?</h1>
      <p class="meta">Updated July 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p class="lead">
      ExpressVPN and NordVPN are the two consumer VPNs most often shortlisted in 2026, and they are not interchangeable. ExpressVPN wins on consistent speeds, reliable streaming unblocking, and app simplicity. NordVPN wins on price, a larger server network, and extra features like double VPN and meshnet. This comparison breaks down speed, server network, privacy, streaming, pricing, and apps so you can pick the right one for your needs.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-top">
      <a href="https://www.expressvpn.com" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try ExpressVPN</a>
      <a href="https://nordvpn.com" class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try NordVPN</a>
    </div>

    <h2>Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Feature</th><th>ExpressVPN</th><th>NordVPN</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Best For</td><td>Speed, streaming, simplicity</td><td>Value, features, server network</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Server Count</td><td>3,000+ in 105 countries</td><td>6,400+ in 111 countries</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Simultaneous Devices</td><td>8</td><td>10</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Price (2-Year)</td><td>$6.67/mo</td><td>$3.39/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Protocols</td><td>Lightway, OpenVPN, IKEv2, L2TP</td><td>NordLynx, OpenVPN, IKEv2</td></tr>
        <tr><td>No-Logs Policy</td><td>Yes, audited</td><td>Yes, audited</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Jurisdiction</td><td>British Virgin Islands</td><td>Panama</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Streaming Unblocking</td><td>Best in class</td><td>Very good</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Double VPN</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Meshnet</td><td>No</td><td>Yes, included</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Split Tunneling</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kill Switch</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>24/7 Live Chat</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Money-back Guarantee</td><td>30 days</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Router App</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What Is ExpressVPN?</h2>
    <p>ExpressVPN is a consumer VPN service founded in 2009 and headquartered in the British Virgin Islands. It was one of the first VPNs to focus on user experience rather than just technical features, and it has built a reputation for consistent speeds, reliable streaming unblocking, and polished apps across every platform. ExpressVPN was acquired by Kape Technologies in 2021 but continues to operate independently under its original team.</p>
    <p>The current version runs on ExpressVPN's proprietary Lightway protocol, which is faster and more lightweight than OpenVPN. ExpressVPN operates 3,000+ servers in 105 countries, supports 8 simultaneous connections, and includes a router app, browser extensions, and a built-in password manager. Pricing starts at $6.67 per month on a 1-year plan with 3 months free, with a 30-day money-back guarantee. ExpressVPN is the choice of users who want a set-and-forget VPN that just works.</p>

    <h2>What Is NordVPN?</h2>
    <p>NordVPN is a consumer VPN service founded in 2012 by four childhood friends and headquartered in Panama. It launched publicly in 2014 and has grown to over 14 million users as of 2026, making it one of the most widely used VPNs in the world. NordVPN's distinguishing feature is its large server network of 6,400+ servers in 111 countries, combined with specialty servers like Double VPN, Obfuscated, and Onion Over VPN.</p>
    <p>The current version runs on NordLynx, NordVPN's implementation of the WireGuard protocol, which is fast and efficient. NordVPN operates 6,400+ servers, supports 10 simultaneous connections, and includes Meshnet for secure device-to-device connections, Threat Protection for ad and malware blocking, and NordPass for password management. Pricing starts at $3.39 per month on a 2-year plan, with a 30-day money-back guarantee. NordVPN is the choice of users who want more features and a larger server network at a lower price.</p>

    <h2>Speed and Performance</h2>
    <p>VPN speed is the single most important factor for daily use. ExpressVPN is generally faster and more consistent, while NordVPN is fast on nearby servers but more variable on long-distance connections.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Speed</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN's Lightway protocol delivers consistent speeds across long distances. Independent speed tests in 2026 show ExpressVPN retaining 85% or more of baseline speeds on international servers, with minimal variance between connections. This consistency matters for video calls, gaming, and large file transfers where drops in speed cause noticeable lag. ExpressVPN also has lower latency than most competitors, which makes it feel more responsive for interactive use.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Speed</h3>
    <p>NordVPN's NordLynx protocol is fast on nearby servers, often matching or exceeding ExpressVPN on domestic connections. However, on long-distance international servers, NordVPN's speed drops more noticeably, retaining 70% to 80% of baseline speeds. NordVPN also has more variance between servers, so you may need to switch servers to find the fastest one. For most users, the difference is not noticeable, but for users who need consistent international speeds, ExpressVPN is better.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span> wins speed and performance consistency.</p>

    <h2>Server Network and Coverage</h2>
    <p>The size and distribution of a VPN's server network affects speed, availability, and the ability to access region-locked content. NordVPN has the larger network.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Servers</h3>
    <p>NordVPN operates 6,400+ servers in 111 countries, the largest network among major consumer VPNs in 2026. The large network means more server options per country, which reduces congestion and improves speed. NordVPN also offers specialty servers like Double VPN for extra encryption, Obfuscated servers for bypassing VPN blocks, and Onion Over VPN for Tor access. For users who need servers in specific countries or want specialty server types, NordVPN has the edge.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Servers</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN operates 3,000+ servers in 105 countries. While the server count is lower than NordVPN, ExpressVPN compensates with consistent performance across its network. ExpressVPN also operates all servers in RAM-only mode, meaning no data is written to disk, which is a strong privacy feature. ExpressVPN covers most countries a typical user would need, but it has fewer options in niche locations compared to NordVPN.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best server count and specialty servers go to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Best server consistency goes to <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span>.</p>

    <h2>Streaming and Unblocking</h2>
    <p>For many users, the main reason to use a VPN is streaming. ExpressVPN is the most reliable at unblocking streaming services.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Streaming</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN is the best VPN for streaming in 2026. It reliably unblocks Netflix US, Netflix UK, Disney+, Hulu, BBC iPlayer, Amazon Prime Video, HBO Max, and more. ExpressVPN's streaming performance is consistent across devices, including smart TVs, streaming sticks, and mobile. The MediaStreamer feature lets you stream on devices that do not support VPNs natively, like Apple TV and some gaming consoles.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Streaming</h3>
    <p>NordVPN also unblocks most major streaming services, including Netflix, Disney+, Hulu, BBC iPlayer, and Amazon Prime Video. However, NordVPN occasionally requires server switching to find a server that works, especially for Netflix US on mobile. NordVPN's SmartPlay feature integrates streaming unblocking into the app, which is convenient. For most streaming needs, NordVPN works well, but ExpressVPN is more reliable.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span> wins streaming and unblocking.</p>

    <h2>Privacy and Security</h2>
    <p>Privacy is the core promise of a VPN. Both ExpressVPN and NordVPN have strong privacy practices, but they differ in jurisdiction and features.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Privacy</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN is headquartered in the British Virgin Islands, which has no data retention laws and is outside the Five Eyes intelligence alliance. ExpressVPN has a strict no-logs policy that has been independently audited by PwC. All servers run in RAM-only mode, meaning all data is wiped when the server reboots. ExpressVPN also uses TrustedServer technology, which ensures the server software is the same across all servers and cannot be modified.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Privacy</h3>
    <p>NordVPN is headquartered in Panama, which also has no data retention laws and is outside the Five Eyes alliance. NordVPN has a strict no-logs policy that has been independently audited by PwC and Deloitte. NordVPN also operates RAM-only servers and offers Double VPN for users who want extra encryption. NordVPN's Threat Protection feature blocks ads, trackers, and malware at the network level, which is a valuable addition.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best jurisdiction and server transparency go to <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span>. Best extra security features like Double VPN go to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>.</p>

    <h2>Pricing Comparison</h2>
    <p>Pricing is where NordVPN has a clear advantage. NordVPN is significantly cheaper than ExpressVPN at every tier.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Tier</th><th>ExpressVPN</th><th>NordVPN</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Monthly</td><td>$12.95/mo</td><td>$12.99/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>6-Month</td><td>$9.99/mo</td><td>Not available</td></tr>
        <tr><td>1-Year</td><td>$6.67/mo (3 months free)</td><td>$4.99/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2-Year</td><td>Not available</td><td>$3.39/mo (3 months free)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Simultaneous Devices</td><td>8</td><td>10</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Money-back Guarantee</td><td>30 days</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Free Trial</td><td>7 days (mobile)</td><td>7 days (mobile)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bundle (Password Manager)</td><td>Yes (ExpressVPN Keys)</td><td>Yes (NordPass add-on)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bundle (Cloud Storage)</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (NordLocker add-on)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Annual Cost (Best Tier)</td><td>$80.04</td><td>$40.68</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>For budget-conscious users, NordVPN at $3.39 per month on a 2-year plan is less than half the cost of ExpressVPN at $6.67 per month on a 1-year plan. Over 2 years, NordVPN costs $81.36 and ExpressVPN costs $160.08, so NordVPN saves you nearly $80.</p>
    <p>For users who want the most polished experience and are willing to pay more, ExpressVPN's higher price is justified by its speed and streaming reliability. For users who want the best value, NordVPN is the clear winner.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best price goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Best value for speed-focused users goes to <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span>.</p>

    <h2>Apps and Ease of Use</h2>
    <p>How the VPN app feels day-to-day matters. ExpressVPN is simpler, while NordVPN is more feature-rich.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Apps</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN's apps are the simplest and most polished in the category. The main screen is a single connect button, with server selection in a clean list. The app works the same way on Windows, Mac, iOS, Android, Linux, and routers, so you only learn the interface once. ExpressVPN also offers browser extensions for Chrome, Firefox, and Edge that control the desktop app. For beginners and non-technical users, ExpressVPN is the easiest VPN to use.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Apps</h3>
    <p>NordVPN's apps are feature-rich, with a map interface for server selection, specialty server categories, and a kill switch. The map interface is visually appealing but can feel cluttered on smaller screens. NordVPN also offers browser extensions, but they function as proxies rather than full VPNs. For power users who want options like Double VPN and Meshnet, NordVPN's apps are more capable. For simplicity, ExpressVPN is better.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best simplicity goes to <span class="winner-tag">ExpressVPN</span>. Best features and options go to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>.</p>

    <h2>Extra Features</h2>
    <p>Beyond core VPN functionality, both services offer extra features. NordVPN has more, while ExpressVPN focuses on doing the basics well.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Extras</h3>
    <p>NordVPN includes Meshnet, which lets you connect your devices securely over a private mesh network, useful for remote access and file sharing. Threat Protection blocks ads, trackers, and malware. Double VPN routes traffic through two servers for extra encryption. Onion Over VPN combines VPN with Tor for maximum anonymity. NordVPN also offers NordPass for password management and NordLocker for encrypted cloud storage as paid add-ons.</p>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Extras</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN includes MediaStreamer, a DNS-based streaming unblocker for devices that do not support VPNs. ExpressVPN Keys is a built-in password manager included with the subscription. ExpressVPN also offers a router app that lets you protect all devices on your network. ExpressVPN does not offer Double VPN, Meshnet, or ad blocking, focusing instead on core VPN performance.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span> wins extra features and value.</p>

    <h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

    <h3>ExpressVPN Pros</h3>
    <div class="pros-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Most consistent speeds across long distances</li>
