        <li>Acquired by Kape Technologies (controversial history)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Who Should Use Which?</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Streamers and Cord-Cutters</h3>
      <p>If your primary use is streaming Netflix, Disney+, Hulu, or BBC iPlayer, ExpressVPN is the better choice. Its streaming unblocking is the most reliable in the category, and it works consistently across devices including smart TVs and streaming sticks. The higher price is justified by the streaming reliability.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Budget-Conscious Users</h3>
      <p>If you want a VPN for general privacy and security at the lowest price, NordVPN is the better choice. At $3.39 per month on a 2-year plan, it is less than half the cost of ExpressVPN and includes more features. For users who do not need the absolute best streaming or speed consistency, NordVPN offers the best value.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Frequent Travelers</h3>
      <p>If you travel internationally and need consistent speeds across long distances, ExpressVPN is the better choice. Its Lightway protocol maintains speeds better than NordVPN on international servers, which matters for video calls, gaming, and large file transfers while abroad.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Privacy Power Users</h3>
      <p>If you want extra security features like Double VPN, Meshnet, and ad blocking, NordVPN is the better choice. Its specialty servers and Threat Protection feature offer more layers of protection than ExpressVPN. For users in restrictive countries who need obfuscated servers, NordVPN is also stronger.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Beginners and Non-Technical Users</h3>
      <p>If you want a VPN that is simple to set up and use, ExpressVPN is the better choice. Its apps are the most polished and easiest to understand, with a single connect button and clean server list. For users who do not want to deal with specialty servers or map interfaces, ExpressVPN is the simplest option.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Real-World Use Cases</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
