    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is ExpressVPN better than NordVPN?</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN is better for users who want the most consistent speeds, the most reliable streaming unblocking, and the simplest apps. NordVPN is better for users who want more features like double VPN and meshnet, a larger server network, and a lower price. For most users in 2026, NordVPN offers better value, while ExpressVPN offers a more polished experience.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, ExpressVPN or NordVPN?</h3>
    <p>NordVPN is significantly cheaper. NordVPN costs $3.39 per month on a 2-year plan, while ExpressVPN costs $6.67 per month on a 1-year plan. Over 2 years, NordVPN costs $81.36 and ExpressVPN costs $160.08, so NordVPN saves you nearly $80. Both offer a 30-day money-back guarantee, so you can try either risk-free.</p>

    <h3>Which VPN is faster, ExpressVPN or NordVPN?</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN is generally faster and more consistent across long distances. Independent speed tests in 2026 show ExpressVPN retaining 85% or more of baseline speeds on international servers, while NordVPN retains 70% to 80%. NordVPN's NordLynx protocol is fast on nearby servers but can be more variable on long-distance connections.</p>

    <h3>Which VPN is better for streaming?</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN is better for streaming. It unblocks Netflix, Disney+, Hulu, BBC iPlayer, and Amazon Prime Video more reliably than NordVPN, especially on mobile and smart TVs. NordVPN also unblocks most streaming services but occasionally requires server switching. For users whose primary use is streaming, ExpressVPN is the safer choice.</p>

    <h3>Can I use ExpressVPN and NordVPN together?</h3>
    <p>You can install both VPNs on the same device, but you can only run one at a time. Running two VPNs simultaneously causes routing conflicts. A practical approach is to use ExpressVPN on your main streaming device and NordVPN on a travel laptop or router, so each device uses a different VPN without conflict.</p>

    <h3>Which VPN has better apps?</h3>
    <p>ExpressVPN has simpler, more polished apps that are easier for beginners. NordVPN has more feature-rich apps with a map interface, specialty servers, and a kill switch, but they can feel cluttered for new users. For simplicity, ExpressVPN wins. For power users who want options, NordVPN wins.</p>

